---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Questions · Direct Lifestyle Medicine" active="questions">

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Questions</h1>
      <p class="lede">If your question isn&rsquo;t here, ask it in the free conversation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="pillbar">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <a href="#model">The model</a>
        <a href="#money">Money &amp; coverage</a>
        <a href="#availability">Availability</a>
        <a href="#medicine">The medicine</a>
        <a href="#starting">Starting &amp; stopping</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="faq-group" id="model">
        <h2>The model</h2>
        <div class="faq">
          <details>
            <summary>What is lifestyle medicine?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              It is medical care that treats the way you live as part of
              the treatment: food, activity, sleep, stress, alcohol and
              tobacco, and the people around you. These drive many common
              conditions, so that is where I start. It is a way of
              practicing medicine, not a separate field.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is this just health coaching?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              No. I am a licensed physician. I examine, diagnose, order
              labs and imaging, prescribe, and treat within my scope.
              Starting with lifestyle does not mean avoiding medicine
              when medicine is what you need.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Do I need to already have a primary care doctor?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              No. Some members have one, and I work alongside them. Some
              don&rsquo;t, and I provide the preventive and medical care
              I can and help them set up anything else they need. You do
              not have to choose between me and another doctor.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Does this replace my regular primary care?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              It depends on what you need. I treat within my scope and
              refer when something is outside it. Some members use me as their only doctor. Some keep a
              primary care doctor and use me for prevention, lifestyle
              work, and coordination. We decide which one fits you.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is this health insurance?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              No. It is a direct agreement between you and me for my
              services as your doctor. Keep your insurance for everything
              else: labs, medicines, specialists, hospitals.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is this &ldquo;concierge medicine&rdquo;?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              It shares one idea with concierge practices: a small panel
              and real access. Concierge fees typically run $2,400 to
              $5,000 a year on top of insurance billing. This is $99 a
              month, I bill no one, and there are no tiers of care.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Why is it only $99 a month? What&rsquo;s the catch?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              The practice is small: no office building, no billing
              department, no staff, and a limited number of patients. The
              limits: I keep business hours. I am not an emergency service. I treat
              within my scope. I take real time away each year. When my
              panel is full, it is full.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How long are visits?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              As long as they need to be. A first visit is up to 90
              minutes. I keep my panel small so I can keep it that way.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="money">
        <h2>Money &amp; coverage</h2>
        <div class="faq">
          <details>
            <summary>Besides $99 a month, what will I pay?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Nothing to me. Care from others is billed by them, usually
              through your insurance: labs, imaging, medicines, vaccines,
              specialists, urgent care, hospitals. Where I can get
              discounted lab pricing, I pass it through at my cost and
              tell you the number first.
              More: <a href="/pricing">Pricing &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Are there extra fees? Forms? Missed visits?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              No. Paperwork is included: disability and FMLA forms,
              letters, prior authorizations. There are no no-show fees.
              The only pass-throughs are procedure supplies at my cost,
              named before the procedure.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>I&rsquo;m on Medicare or Medicaid. Can I join?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              I want to be able to serve you. How a direct membership
              works with these programs is not settled yet. Ask me in the
              free conversation and I will tell you where it stands. What
              I can say now: I do not bill Medicare, Medicaid, or any
              insurer for my services.
              More: <a href="/pricing">Pricing &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I pay with my HSA or FSA?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Possibly. It depends on how the practice is finally
              structured, which is not settled yet. Confirm with your tax
              advisor, and ask me what I know at the time.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What if $99 a month is out of reach?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Tell me. I offer reduced-rate memberships based on your
              finances, and a small number of free memberships. The
              medical care is the same at every level. There is no
              application, and you do not need to prove anything to
              ask.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="availability">
        <h2>Availability</h2>
        <div class="faq">
          <details>
            <summary>How fast do you respond to messages?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Within 1&ndash;2 business days, often sooner. If something
              needs attention sooner, say so in the message. Do not use
              messages for urgent problems or emergencies.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What about nights, weekends, and emergencies?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              I keep business hours, Monday through Friday. Emergencies
              like chest pain, stroke signs, severe injury, or thoughts
              of self-harm are always 911 and the ER. For urgent same-day
              problems when I&rsquo;m unavailable, use urgent care, then
              tell me.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What happens when you are away?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              I take real time away each year. You will know in advance.
              I still check incoming results and messages for anything
              important. Refills are arranged before I go. Emergencies
              and urgent problems are handled the same way as always. Away means
              slower, never unaware.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Do you make home visits?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Yes. When you need a hands-on exam and live within my
              service area, I come to you, scheduled ahead, at no extra
              charge. Most care is by video, with a clinic when a
              procedure needs an equipped room.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="medicine">
        <h2>The medicine</h2>
        <div class="faq">
          <details>
            <summary>What do you treat?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Prevention and screening, and the lifestyle work underneath
              most common conditions. Alongside that: blood pressure,
              diabetes and prediabetes, cholesterol, thyroid, obesity and
              weight (including weight-loss medicines), sleep problems,
              everyday illness, and depression, anxiety, and ADHD within
              primary care. Some conditions need a specialist leading,
              and I will tell you when yours does.
              More: <a href="/help">What I help with &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What is your training, exactly?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              M.D. from the Texas A&amp;M College of Medicine. Internal
              medicine internship at George Washington University.
              Primary care at a community health center, alongside
              leading NIH-funded research on aging and health
              technology. Lifestyle medicine
              board certification expected January 2027. I did not
              complete a residency. The full picture:
              <a href="/about">About &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Do you prescribe controlled medicines?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Yes, under a written policy, including ADHD medicines when
              appropriate. Federal and Texas telemedicine
              rules apply, some medicines require in-person evaluation or
              monitoring, and I prescribe conservatively. If your main
              goal is a specific controlled prescription, I am probably
              not the right fit.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What if I need a specialist or the hospital?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              I refer you to the right specialist and stay involved. In the hospital, the hospital&rsquo;s
              doctors lead. I stay informed and manage your care when you
              are home.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="starting">
        <h2>Starting &amp; stopping</h2>
        <div class="faq">
          <details>
            <summary>What is the free conversation like?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Thirty minutes by video. You tell me what is going on. I
              ask questions and tell you if I can help. To book, you give
              only your name, email, and phone. There is no bill.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How do I join, and how fast can we start?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              After we talk: sign the membership agreement, set up
              payment, and schedule your first full visit. It is usually
              within two weeks, after I have read any records you have.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is there a contract or minimum commitment?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              No. Month to month from day one, no enrollment fee, cancel
              anytime, effective at the end of your billing month. Full
              terms: <a href="/agreement">the membership agreement
              &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What happens to my records if I leave?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              They are yours. A complete electronic copy is always free
              and sent promptly to you and your next doctor. Active
              issues are handed off safely, and prescriptions are bridged
              up to 90 days where clinically safe.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can my spouse or family join?</summary>
            <p class="a">
              Any adult can join, each with their own membership at the
              same $99. A couple is $198 a month. I care for adults
              only, so children need a pediatrician.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Closing CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Still have a question? Ask me.</h2>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
